322 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 135 0 R
/E (In conclusion, we found a Raspberry Pi device that was hacked because it was using default credentials. The attacker used Telnet to break in and then controlled the device remotely from a C2 server. We fixed everything by disabling Telnet, enabling SSH, blocking the attacker's IP, and isolating the device in VLAN 20. All our security tests passed. The network is now safe. The most important lesson here is simple: always change default passwords.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
